docs {
  ## Checkout Story
  
  Initiates a Stripe checkout session to unlock a specific story for the authenticated user.
  
  This endpoint requires a valid JWT bearer token.
  
  ### Path Parameters
  
  | Field | Type   | Constraints | Description                        |
  |-------|--------|-------------|------------------------------------|
  | `id`  | string | UUID v4     | The unique ID of the story to buy. |
  
  ### Success Response — `201 Created`
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "story checkout session successfully",
    "data": {
      "url": "https://checkout.stripe.com/c/pay/cs_test_a1b2c3d4e5f67890"
    },
    "meta": null
  }
  ```
  
  ### Error Responses
  
  #### `400 Bad Request` — Invalid UUID
  
  Returned when the `:id` path parameter is not a valid UUID format.
  
  ```json
  {
    "statusCode": 400,
    "message": "Validation failed (uuid is expected)",
    "error": "Bad Request"
  }
  ```
  
  #### `401 Unauthorized` — Missing or Invalid JWT
  
  Returned when no bearer token is provided or the token is invalid/expired.
  
  ```json
  {
    "statusCode": 401,
    "message": "Unauthorized"
  }
  ```
  
  #### `404 Not Found` — Story Not Found
  
  Returned when no story matches the given ID for the authenticated user.
  
  ```json
  {
    "statusCode": 404,
    "message": "Story a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890 not found",
    "error": "Not Found"
  }
  ```
}
